Vendored RIFE model architecture — attribution
================================================

The frame-interpolation model architecture in this directory
(ifnet_hdv3.py, warplayer.py) is derived from the Practical-RIFE project:

    Practical-RIFE / RIFE: Real-Time Intermediate Flow Estimation
    Author:  hzwer (Zhewei Huang) and contributors
    Source:  https://github.com/hzwer/Practical-RIFE
             https://github.com/hzwer/ECCV2022-RIFE
    License: MIT (see LICENSE in this directory)

Paper:
    Huang, Z., Zhang, T., Heng, W., Shi, B., Zhou, S.
    "Real-Time Intermediate Flow Estimation for Video Frame Interpolation."
    ECCV 2022.

What is vendored here
---------------------
Only the model ARCHITECTURE (pure PyTorch nn.Module code) is vendored — this
is the HDv3 IFNet variant. The trained weights (`flownet.pkl`) are NOT
committed to this repository. They are fetched at setup time by
`scripts/setup_rife.py` from a pinned, MIT-licensed HuggingFace mirror of the
upstream Practical-RIFE weights (default: AlexWortega/RIFE, a verified mirror
whose 160-tensor state dict loads into ifnet_hdv3.py with strict=True). The
mirror repo, file and revision are all env-configurable — see settings.py.

Reproducibility note
--------------------
Upstream distributes weights only via Google Drive / Baidu, which cannot be
used for automated/clean-install setup. Pinning a HuggingFace mirror revision
makes `pnpm setup:rife` deterministic and scriptable.
